# Documentation

Update the owning doc in the same change as the behavior.

| Change | Doc |
|--------|-----|
| Domain term | `GLOSSARY.md` |
| Hard-to-reverse trade-off | `docs/adr/` |
| Assessment system design (diagram, observability, GenAI design) | `docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md` |
| AI collaboration narrative (step-by-step) | `docs/AI_COLLABORATION.md` |
| System shape | `docs/architecture/README.md` |
| Endpoint or envelope | `docs/architecture/api-outline.md` |
| Table, column, index | `docs/architecture/database-schema.md` |
| Package layout | `docs/architecture/directory-structure.md` |
| FE integration policy | `docs/architecture/frontend-integration.md` |
| Page ↔ API ↔ hook | `docs/architecture/frontend-backend-mapping.md` |
| UI stack or routes | `docs/architecture/inventory-frontend.md` |
| Bootstrap, ports, Compose | `README.md` |

Mark a route **planned** until it exists in `routes.go`. Samples (aging threshold, enums, JSON) match the code. A new convention also updates `.cursor/rules/`.
